          "The first account concerns a man named Micah, who lived in the hill country of Ephraim. He confessed to his mother that he had taken a large amount of silver from her. She responded by blessing him in the name of the Lord, but the household then used part of the silver to make an image. Micah established a shrine, made religious objects, and appointed one of his sons as a priest.",
