          "A group from the tribe of Dan then travelled through the region seeking territory. They took Micah’s religious objects and persuaded his priest to go with them. They later attacked Laish, a peaceful and unsuspecting community, killed its inhabitants, burned the city, and rebuilt it as their own settlement. They established the stolen religious objects there.",
          "The narrative connects this behaviour with the repeated theme that Israel had no king and people did what was right in their own eyes. Their actions were not shaped by faithful obedience to God and justice toward their neighbours. Religious symbols had become objects to possess, while the lives and rights of other people were treated as obstacles.",
