          "After the fighting, the Israelites faced another crisis: the near destruction of the tribe of Benjamin. They had made an oath not to give their daughters in marriage to Benjamin, and they sought ways to preserve the tribe without breaking their oath. The solutions described in Judges 21 involved further violence and the seizure of women, adding injustice to the earlier tragedy.",
          "These chapters are among the darkest in the Bible. The text records the actions of people and communities that have abandoned justice, but recording an action is not the same as endorsing it. The treatment of the concubine, the attack on Laish, and the seizure of women must be recognised as acts of severe harm, not examples for Christian communities to imitate.",
